TC05 - Local TLS fail-closed runtime checks
Date: 2026-11-27 (local time, UTC+07:00)
Target: Server on loopback TCP 9000; isolated DanToPhongDB_Test
Certificate: short-lived self-signed test certificate with localhost SAN; stored outside the repository and not imported into a system trust store

1. TLS client to TLS server: PASS
   TLS 1.3 handshake completed with the configured certificate pin. A framed PING reached the application and was rejected as unauthenticated (ERR_UNAUTHORIZED).
2. Plaintext client to TLS server: PASS
   A valid length-prefixed JSON PING sent without TLS received no application response; the TLS server closed the connection.
3. TLS client with a mismatched certificate pin: PASS
   The client-side certificate validation callback rejected the server certificate and the TLS handshake failed.
4. Plaintext client to explicitly plaintext server: PASS
   With DANTOPHONG_USE_TLS=false, the loopback-only server accepted a framed plaintext PING and returned the expected ERR_UNAUTHORIZED application response.

The four transport outcomes were observed directly against the running server. No database credential, connection string, certificate fingerprint, token, or OTP is included. This verifies local transport behavior only; it is not evidence of GUI login, remote reachability, or packet-capture inspection.
